    "title": "What Is a Crushing Plant? Components, Working & Applications",
    "excerpt": "A crushing plant is a complete material-processing system designed to reduce large rocks, stones, minerals and other bulk materials into smaller, controlled sizes. Instead of relying on a single crusher, a crushing plant combines equipment such as feeders, crushers, vibrating screens, conveyors, hoppers and control systems to move material through different stages of processing.\n",
    "desc": "A crushing plant is a complete material-processing system designed to reduce large rocks, stones, minerals and other bulk materials into smaller, controlled sizes. Instead of relying on a single crusher, a crushing plant combines equipment such as feeders, crushers, vibrating screens, conveyors, hoppers and control systems to move material through different stages of processing.\n",
